{{quote|The lords of the quasielementals keep themselves secreted away from the eyes of all others. No powers live in the plane of Steam. There is only one major player in the whole plane. '''Xanxost''': Xanxost is a slaad. What is a slaad doing in the Inner Planes? No one knows. Wait, that has been said. No major players.|Xanxost}}
'''Xanxost''' is a blue [[slaad]]<ref name="foe9">{{b|Planescape|Faces of Evil: The Fiends|pdf=121100|page=9}}</ref> who enjoys travelling the planes, with his primary motivation apparently the consumption of other creatures he encounters. He writes reports of his exploits, which occasionally get published. Xanxost has variously gone by "it/its" (Ice the Thrice-Born) and "he/his" (Inner Planes Editor) pronouns; it fluctuates depending on the speaker, as one might expect from a creature of chaos. It's not known if Xanxost cares or has even noticed.
Xanxost compiled information about the [[tanar'ri]] (specifically rankings, vulnerabilities, and [[Abyssal lord]]s), [[imp]]s, and [[quasit]]s for [[Ice the Thrice-Born]]'s ''[[Faces of Evil: The Fiends|Faces of Evil]]'', and the [[Quasi-Elemental Plane of Steam]] for an unnamed editor's guide to [[The Inner Planes]].
Xanxost delights in recounting his travels to "mortals", but seems to have difficulty counting.
== Background Information == * Xanxost was created by [[Ray Vallese]], and quickly became a fan favorite, despite his relatively late appearance in the Planescape game line and the fact that he only appears twice, officially. * Ray runs an X/Twitter account for Xanxost: [https://x.com/RealXanxost @RealXanxost]
